"""Crash-safe, append-only quota custody for read-only source sensors.

The ledger is deliberately narrower than a provider adapter.  It stores only
content commitments and bounded, privacy-safe control material.  It has no
network, credential resolver, environment lookup, implicit clock, default
database path, CONTACT/WRITE/SPEND authority, or raw provider payload seam.

Every mutation runs under ``BEGIN IMMEDIATE`` and appends an immutable event.
A reservation is durable before dispatch.  Until an accepted page or an exact
reconciliation is committed, its full item/byte quota remains held.  A process
crash therefore fails closed: reopening yields ``RECONCILE_ONLY`` work and
never authorizes a blind retry.

An optional, explicitly injected monotonic anchor can pin every changing event
head.  The module neither implements a network client nor accepts caller-made
anchor hashes on mutation methods: trust enters only through the injected
``SourceReadExternalAnchor`` boundary.  An anchor/local commit tear, a stale
anchor, or an old database substituted at the same path is quarantined rather
than guessed through.  Stores created without that boundary remain local-only.

Quota epochs may change only through a separately evidenced, anchor-backed
transition after all prior custody is final and only when the exact governed
policy is continuous.  Reconciliation quarantine is append-only and retains
the complete quota hold.  None of these controls make live release eligible.
"""

